course: dictionary
lesson: 12158
title: Words that complete each other
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Complement is a word with several meanings, but they share one idea: something goes with another thing and makes it better or complete. «The red scarf complements her green coat.» The scarf goes well with the coat and makes the outfit look finished.
explain: When two things complement each other, each one makes the other better. «Hot soup and warm bread complement each other.» Neither one needs the other to be food, but together they taste better.
explain: Complement can also mean something different in maths and grammar. In maths, two angles that add up to 90 degrees are complements of each other. In grammar, a complement is a word that finishes a sentence's meaning. Check the subject first: is it about food and clothes, numbers, or sentences?
fact: To complement something is to go well with it and make it better or complete.
fact: A complement is something that goes well with another thing and completes it.
fact: A full complement is the whole number needed, such as «a full crew of twenty sailors».
fact: Complementary angles add up to 90 degrees, and each one is the complement of the other.
fact: In grammar, a complement completes the meaning after verbs like «be», as in «She is a doctor».
exercise: «The mint sauce complements the lamb.» What does complements mean here? | Argues with it and spoils it | Is the same colour as it | *Goes well with it and makes it better | Costs more than it
exercise: «Angles of 30 and 60 degrees are complementary: they add up to 90 degrees.» What is the complement of 30 degrees? | 90 degrees | 30 degrees | *60 degrees | 120 degrees
exercise: «A full complement of players was on the pitch.» What does full complement mean? | A team with a few players missing | A kind of pitch | *The whole number needed | A very large crowd
test: «Hot soup and warm bread complement each other.» What does complement each other mean? | *Go well together and make each other better | Are always eaten in a fight | Are both cold | Cost the same price
test: In «She is a doctor», what does the word doctor do? | Joins two sentences | Shows an action | Names a colour | *Completes the meaning after is
exam: In «complementary angles», what do the two angles add up to? | 45 degrees | 360 degrees | *90 degrees | 180 degrees
